\section{Subsystem Specifications}

\subsection{Tier 1: User Interface \& Visualization Layer}

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Framework:} Qt6/QML with embedded WebGL viewport.
\item \textbf{Telemetry Streaming:} ZeroMQ pub-sub channels at 60 FPS.
\item \textbf{Control Binding:} Real-time modification of O/F ratios and
      chamber pressure targets.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Tier 2: Core Computational Engine}

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Threading Runtime:} Intel TBB distributing tasks across 32+ cores.
\item \textbf{Solver Pipeline:} Implicit BDF + adaptive RKF45 integrators.
\item \textbf{Data Storage:} HDF5 ring buffers exceeding 2.4 GB/s throughput.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Tier 3: Hardware-in-the-Loop \& Containment Layer}

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Thermal Protection:} Ta$_4$HfC$_5$ matrix with CNT reinforcement.
\item \textbf{Plasma Confinement:} REBCO HTS toroidal-cusp magnetic barrier.
\item \textbf{Active Damping:} PZT micro-actuators neutralizing combustion
      instabilities up to 50 kHz.
\end{itemize}

\section{Summary}

This structural blueprint defines the complete system hierarchy of the
STME-RS-A propulsion framework, integrating visualization, simulation,
and hardware subsystems into a cohesive engineering architecture.